Voice Answers for WaniKani: Unofficial Tool
Patch notes: from 0.1.2 (the first listed version, 2026-10-05) to 0.4.2

As always: speech recognition runs entirely on your device, the add-on
makes no network requests, the question is never read, and a wrong answer
goes in exactly as you said it.

Accuracy numbers below are from real recordings of WaniKani items:
300 English meanings and 400 readings.


0.4.2 (upcoming store release)
------------------------------
Readings
- Impossible kana are never offered: a small ゃ/ゅ/ょ after anything but an
  i-row kana (ゆゅ, んょ), two small kana in a row, っ before a vowel.
  Right reading first: 163 -> 166 of 400. None of WaniKani's 6,924 readings
  is affected.
- ず/づ and じ/ぢ sound the same, so the other spelling is offered as a
  choice too (つずく -> つづく, ちじむ -> ちぢむ).

More choices
- Settings -> Answers offered: 1 to 5 choices, set separately for English
  and readings (default 3). At 5, the right reading is among the choices
  for 288 of 400 recordings (270 at 3).

WaniKani dictionary (optional, off by default)
- Answers that are the meaning or reading of any WaniKani item (any level,
  plus your own synonyms; never just the current question) are offered
  first. Nothing you said is replaced.
- Right answer first: readings 166 -> 248 of 400, meanings 242 -> 259 of 300.
- The add-on still never goes online: you make the dictionary file with
  tools/wk-dictionary.mjs from the source repository, using your own
  WaniKani API token (about 15 requests, within WaniKani's rate limit),
  and choose it in Settings -> WaniKani dictionary.

Ignore a wrong answer (optional, off by default)
- Submitted the wrong choice by accident? While the answer is red, press
  Escape or Backspace, or tap Ignore on the panel. The question comes back
  unanswered, and WaniKani doesn't count the mistake: its count, the
  item's place in the queue and the session score are put back as they
  were. Works like the Double-Check script's re-type, and stays out of the
  way when Double-Check is installed.
- An answer you ignored isn't offered again for that question.
- No auto-advance past a wrong answer that can still be ignored.

Settings
- Test mode (typing instead of speaking) is no longer offered in the
  settings. If you had it on, the update switches back to speech.


0.3.3
-----
- More accurate English (fast, Moonshine, the default): its encoder runs in
  float16 instead of 8-bit. Right answer first: 237 -> 242 of 300; among
  the choices: 267 -> 271. About 0.04 s slower per answer; the download is
  about 20 MB larger.
- Custom models can say which precision each part is in, so a
  full-precision English model can be loaded (a ready-made one,
  moonshine-base-fp32.wkv-model.zip, is on the GitHub releases page: 246
  of 300 right first time). Model files made for earlier versions still
  work.


0.3.1
-----
Better recognition with the built-in models (Moonshine, right answer first:
227 -> 237 of 300):
- Say it again: if you record over an answer (or tap Clear), it isn't
  offered again for that question. If only it is heard again, the panel
  says so instead of auto-submitting it.
- English alternatives can differ in any word, not just the first, and are
  ranked by how likely the whole answer is.
- Words that sound alike are offered too (eye / I, tail / tale, son / sun).
- A bare "and", "so" or "that" ranks a little lower, so "hand" is no longer
  heard as "and".
- Readings: alternatives are checked against the clip at three speeds
  (right reading among the choices: 253 -> 270 of 400), and the ー spelling
  no longer takes the second choice.
- Push-to-talk keeps recording 0.2 s after you let go, so the end of a word
  isn't cut off.
- A hesitation ("um") is never turned into an answer.

Microphone
- By default the microphone stays open between answers so the start of
  your answer isn't cut off: the last 0.3 s sits in memory, constantly
  overwritten, and is used only when you press. New setting to turn this
  off (the microphone then opens only while you hold the key or button).
  The privacy policy now describes this exactly.


0.2.7
-----
- Renamed "Voice Answers for WaniKani: Unofficial Tool", following
  WaniKani's branding guidelines; the settings page says it's an
  unofficial tool, not affiliated with WaniKani or Tofugu.


0.2.3 - 0.2.6
-------------
Firefox for Android
- Everything works by touch: hold the panel's mic button to talk (let go
  away from it to cancel), with Submit, Clear and Next buttons.
- On phones the panel is a bar at the bottom of the screen with
  finger-sized buttons, and it stays above the on-screen keyboard.
- The microphone uses Android's automatic gain (a phone's raw microphone is
  far quieter than a desktop's).

Chrome and Chromium browsers (Edge, Brave, ...)
- The add-on is on the Chrome Web Store, with the same features and the
  same on-device recognition.

Faster English
- Moonshine is the new default ("fast"): about 0.1 s per answer on a
  desktop and 0.3 s on a phone. Whisper base.en stays available as
  "accurate" (about 1.5 s / 4 s).
- A word or phrase the recogniser repeats ("king king", "barbar") is
  collapsed to one.

Custom models
- English models fine-tuned on your own voice (Moonshine or Whisper) can be
  loaded in the settings, as reading models already could. Tools to
  fine-tune on your voice are in the source repository.

Smaller things
- The settings page shows the version number, and its wording no longer
  assumes Firefox.
- Choosing a model file from the toolbar popup now works (it opens the
  settings in a tab), and a model file for the wrong language says where
  it goes.
- The pause button moved: pause in the settings or with Alt+Shift+V;
  pressing the mic while paused turns voice answers back on.
